<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="skill">ranged-combat</ansi> skill

The <ansi fg="skill">ranged-combat</ansi> skill governs your proficiency
with ranged weapons: bows, crossbows, pistols, and slings.
Higher ranks improve your hit chance and damage at range.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Aimed Shots ━━━</ansi>

Ranged weapons shoot with the <ansi fg="command">fire</ansi> command. Every shot
is a deliberate aimed action: accuracy and damage both scale
with <ansi fg="stat">Perception</ansi>, not Strength. A keen eye matters
more than raw muscle.

Firing readies the next round by itself, so there is no second
command to remember. Each shot draws one round from a bundle of
arrows, bolts, or shot carried in your pack, and you are told
when you spend the last of them.

Firing spends Stamina and requires full payment. Your carried
load raises the price, while <ansi fg="skill">ranged-combat</ansi> skill lowers
it. If you are too spent, the action refuses before a shot, ammunition, or
cooldown is consumed.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Range ━━━</ansi>

  - <ansi fg="stat">Same room:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">fire <target></ansi>
  - <ansi fg="stat">Adjacent room:</ansi> <ansi fg="command">fire <target> <direction></ansi>
      Cross-room fire does not pull you into melee. The target
      must close the distance to engage in melee combat.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ A Clear Shot ━━━</ansi>

An archer does far more harm when nothing in the room is attacking
them. You cannot steady an aimed shot while you are fending someone
off, and the shot is much the weaker for it. Keep a companion, a party
member, or a room between you and whatever wants to reach you.

A shot from hiding at something in your own room is an
<ansi fg="magenta-bold">ambush</ansi>: heavier, answerable, and it costs you your
special move and your cover. Firing into the next room is never an
ambush, and it leaves your cover intact. See
<ansi fg="command">help ambush</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Progression ━━━</ansi>

This skill improves through use:
  - Landing shots with a ranged weapon
  - Perception advances from aimed-shot attacks

